// lexdb over TNS: the bugs the user documentation found in the Oracle door (KNOWN-ISSUES.md, the bug-fix slice), checked against Oracle Database Free 23.26
// (gen_oracle.py --check tns_docbugs; the known differences are in oracle_known_diffs.txt): an INSERT ... SELECT, UPDATE and MERGE into a table with a
// foreign key and a CHECK that a row fails part way (ORA-02290, ORA-02291), DROP COLUMN of a column in a multi-column CHECK (ORA-12991) and of one in a
// single-column CHECK (the check goes), ENABLE and DISABLE of a key, a name not there (ORA-02430, ORA-02431), ADD CONSTRAINT over rows that break it
// (ORA-02293, ORA-02298, ORA-02437, ORA-02299), a second foreign key on the same columns (ORA-02275 in ALTER TABLE, ORA-02274 in CREATE TABLE), QUALIFY
// (after CONNECT BY, a number or a text as the condition, FOR UPDATE ORA-01786, ORDER BY or FOR UPDATE before it ORA-03049), a package that has only a
// specification, SYS_CONTEXT and NLS_SESSION_PARAMETERS after ALTER SESSION SET CURRENT_SCHEMA, NLS_TERRITORY, NLS_LANGUAGE and NLS_DATE_FORMAT, and a
// DEFAULT that calls a sequence gone (ORA-02289, only for the row that takes the default). Each statement runs with set lexdb_batch = off (the row
// engine) and on: "same" and the answer, or DIFFERENT and both.
